---

kuna (crates/kuna-base, crates/kuna-num, crates/kuna-sleigh, crates/kuna-slacomp)

The vendored crates under crates/ are borrowed from kuna
(https://github.com/Noelo-Lab/kuna), Copyright 2026 The kuna Authors,
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0, at pinned commit
0096e984d74846e45f42c1dbe1fb95252083dda2 (upstream HEAD at vendoring time).
kuna is itself derived from Ghidra
(https://github.com/NationalSecurityAgency/ghidra): the SLEIGH compiler
(kuna-slacomp, the sleigh_opt equivalent) and the SLEIGH runtime types
(kuna-sleigh / kuna-base / kuna-num) are a Rust rendition of Ghidra's C++
decompiler and SLEIGH sources. Per-file `// Ghidra:` anchors inside the
vendored sources point at the upstream C++ file/line each module follows.

The following attribution is reproduced from kuna's NOTICE file:

    kuna

    Portions of the structuring and region-recovery code are ported from angr
    (https://github.com/angr/angr), released under the BSD 2-Clause License.

    (Full text: https://github.com/angr/angr/blob/master/LICENSE)

No angr-derived structuring/region-recovery code is included in the vendored
subset (only kuna-base/kuna-num/kuna-sleigh/kuna-slacomp; the attribution is
carried for provenance completeness of the upstream tree).

Vendoring shape: crate sources (src/) and manifests only; kuna's own
integration-test trees (tests/) and its vendored Ghidra processor-spec corpus
are not included. Rudra's .slaspec inputs always come from the locked Ghidra
12.0.4 oracle tree (see tools/build_locked_x86_64_sla.sh). A small number of
#[cfg(test)] unit tests inside the vendored sources reference kuna's
repo-root datatest corpus that is not vendored; they are inert for Rudra's
gates (which exercise the root package) and are skipped in practice.
